Z||000005||theogre||11-04-2000||09:26 PM||||Are you guys sure, those of you above who aren't being silly, that you don't have a fuel leak someplace. A car sucking that much gas usually runs like crap and/or has heavy black smoke out the back. The V6's high fuel pressure makes a leak a real posibility, but even the 4 can do it if a line rots or is loose a hair.<P>At my worst, with a cracked exhaust manifold screwing up the O2 sensor, I got 23+mpg from my 4 cyl. I usually get anywhere from about 25-32 depending on how much crappy traffic I get stuck in.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||11-04-2000||09:57 PM||||My 5-speed formula averaged 23 mpg in the city and 29 on the highway and that was with spirited driving. My 87 coupe averaged 25 all together and it was a crappie three speed automatic. There is something definitely wrong with your fieros. You should be getting better mileage than that. I would check for exhaust leaks, lazy 02 sensor, Bad tps sensor, and your coolant temperature sensor. I would also check for an out of range map sensor, vacuum leaks, and the engines vacuum also, which should be at least 18 inches at idle.<P><BR>Don't forget that an engine that is out of tune and has tires low on pressure will also aversely effect your mileage. Just because the computer doesn't pick up any codes doesn't mean there isn't a bad component.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||11-04-2000||11:35 PM||||Wow, I thought I was the only one getting bad milage. I get about 6-9, usally almost on E at 100 miles on a tank. I dont drive the car on the highway much, but I get bad milage there too. It an 86 GT 2.8 auto, driver has a heavy foot. I just replaced the map sensor after getting a code. I havent driven it since. I took the intake manifold off a couple weeks ago and it also had that black oily/gas smelling crap all over it. I am going to clean it very throughly before reinstalling. Fuel filter has been replaced recently. I am putting on Rodneys steel vacuum line setup. Is there any way to tell if the TPS is bad by testing it?<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">   <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>If you smoke after sex, your doing it way to fast.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000008||HAGS||11-05-2000||02:26 AM||||When I was getting 4 MPG I was living in Round Rock/Austin with my brother...I worked across the street(farther than it sounds), and I would eat breakfast/shop across the highway...add in one of the worst intersections and you get 4 MPG...<P>My total driving area was probably a 2 square mile radius.  <P>My drive up down to Floresvill I filled up the tank and ran out before I got home...that would be 120 miles... divided by 10 I get 12 MPG...highway...going 90 the whole way and lights up...maybe 1-2 miles of traffic jam in downtown austin||||reg||1
